TI  - Global dynamics of a time-delayed nonlocal reaction-diffusion model of within-host viral infections
AU  - Li, Zhimin
AU  - Zhao, Xiao-Qiang
T2  - Journal of Mathematical Biology
AB  - In this paper, we study a time-delayed nonlocal reaction-diffusion model of withinhost viral infections. We introduce the basic reproduction number R0 and show that the infection-free steady state is globally asymptotically stable when R0 ≤ 1, while the disease is uniformly persistent when R0 > 1. In the case where all coefﬁcients and reaction terms are spatially homogeneous, we obtain an explicit formula of R0 and the global attractivity of the positive constant steady state. Numerically, we illustrate the analytical results, conduct sensitivity analysis, and investigate the impact of drugs on curtailing the spread of the viruses.
