TI  - Multistrain virus dynamics with mutations: a global analysis
AU  - De Leenheer, Patrick
AU  - Pilyugin, Sergei S.
T2  - Mathematical Medicine and Biology: A Journal of the IMA
AB  - We consider within-host virus models with n ≥ 2 strains and allow mutation between the strains. If there is no mutation, a Lyapunov function establishes global stability of the steady state corresponding to the fittest strain. For small perturbations, this steady state persists, perhaps with small concentrations of some or all other strains, depending on the connectivity of the graph describing all possible mutations. Moreover, using a perturbation result due to Smith &amp; Waltman (1999), we show that this steady state also preserves global stability.
